      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.04,
          "end": 4.44,
          "en": "For this here, in the signup screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.44,
          "end": 8.75,
          "en": "we can add a new function, the signupHandler, let's say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.75,
          "end": 13.18,
          "en": "and then that function, we wanna call, \"createUser\".",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 16.03,
          "end": 19.54,
          "en": "Of course, for that, we actually need to export",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 19.54,
          "end": 22.09,
          "en": "this createUser function as a first step.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 22.09,
          "end": 25.96,
          "en": "So, export createUser here in the auth.js file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 25.96,
          "end": 27.89,
          "en": "and then, here, in the signupHandler",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 27.89,
          "end": 31.05,
          "en": "in the signup screen, you can call createUser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 31.05,
          "end": 35.26,
          "en": "and import it from the util auth file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 35.26,
          "end": 37.44,
          "en": "Now the signup handler should be connected",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 37.44,
          "end": 38.75,
          "en": "to the auth content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.75,
          "end": 42.423,
          "en": "because that is where we gather all the user input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 43.81,
          "end": 46.47,
          "en": "Actually, here in AuthContent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 46.47,
          "end": 50.76,
          "en": "we do expect to get an onAuthenticate prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 50.76,
          "end": 53.72,
          "en": "and that onAuthenticate prop will be triggered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 53.72,
          "end": 57.4,
          "en": "whenever the form is submitted with valid data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 57.4,
          "end": 60.14,
          "en": "and then an object with email and password",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 60.14,
          "end": 62.65,
          "en": "will be passed to onAuthenticate.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 62.65,
          "end": 66.483,
          "en": "So to the function received on that onAuthenticate prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 67.41,
          "end": 70.73,
          "en": "We can utilize that fact by going back to the signup screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 70.73,
          "end": 74.78999999999999,
          "en": "and adding the onAuthenticate prop to AuthContent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 74.78999999999999,
          "end": 77.33,
          "en": "and pointing at our signupHandler here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 77.33,
          "end": 79.85,
          "en": "So at this function here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 79.85,
          "end": 82.17,
          "en": "This function will the receive an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 82.17,
          "end": 84.75,
          "en": "that contains email and password, as we just saw,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 84.75,
          "end": 87.74,
          "en": "and we can therefore use object destructuring",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 87.74,
          "end": 91.72,
          "en": "to pull that email and password out of this object here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 91.72,
          "end": 93.65,
          "en": "And the email and password we get here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 93.65,
          "end": 95.84,
          "en": "will have been validated already",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 95.84,
          "end": 99.57300000000001,
          "en": "because we have that validation code in AuthContent JS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 100.44,
          "end": 104.33,
          "en": "As a brief side note, Firebase requires passwords that are",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 104.33,
          "end": 106.21000000000001,
          "en": "at least six characters long.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 106.21000000000001,
          "end": 109.453,
          "en": "That is I have this validation here in AuthContent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 111.75,
          "end": 114.18,
          "en": "Now, with that said, back in Signup Screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 114.18,
          "end": 115.467,
          "en": "we got the email and the password,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 115.467,
          "end": 117.703,
          "en": "and we can now forward this to createUser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 119.86,
          "end": 122.54,
          "en": "Now, as we learned, createUser returns a promise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 122.54,
          "end": 124.69,
          "en": "because we're using async await there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 124.69,
          "end": 126.86,
          "en": "and therefore we might also wanna await",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 126.86,
          "end": 128.52,
          "en": "that promise to resolve",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 128.52,
          "end": 130.423,
          "en": "so that we can show a loading spinner.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 131.32,
          "end": 134.35,
          "en": "Therefore, I'll convert this into async function as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 134.35,
          "end": 138.14,
          "en": "and await my createUser call here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 138.14,
          "end": 140.95,
          "en": "and then we can manage some loading state here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 140.95,
          "end": 144.03,
          "en": "in Signup Screen, with help of useState,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 144.03,
          "end": 146.313,
          "en": "which is imported from React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 147.41,
          "end": 151.02,
          "en": "Now here, I wanna manage some loading state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 151.02,
          "end": 153.733,
          "en": "So I will name this \"isAuthenticating\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 154.79,
          "end": 158.62,
          "en": "and \"setIsAuthenticating\", because that's what we're doing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 158.62,
          "end": 162.39,
          "en": "we are authenticating once the form was submitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 162.39,
          "end": 164.06,
          "en": "And, initially, that is false,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 164.06,
          "end": 165.82999999999998,
          "en": "because when the screen first loads,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 165.82999999999998,
          "end": 168.09,
          "en": "we are not authenticating yet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 168.09,
          "end": 170.65,
          "en": "but once the signupHandler is executed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 170.65,
          "end": 175.65,
          "en": "as a first step, we can set isAuthenticating to true,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 175.84,
          "end": 177.92000000000002,
          "en": "and once we're done creating the user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 177.92000000000002,
          "end": 181.053,
          "en": "we can set isAuthenticating to false here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 181.89,
          "end": 184.49,
          "en": "Now we also might wanna add some error handling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 184.49,
          "end": 186.81,
          "en": "but we'll do this in a second step.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 186.81,
          "end": 189.91,
          "en": "For a first step, I just wanna send this request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 189.91,
          "end": 191.993,
          "en": "and add some loading state management.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 193.115,
          "end": 196.52,
          "en": "Now, we can use this loading state, right here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 196.52,
          "end": 199.52,
          "en": "before we return our JSX content,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 199.52,
          "end": 202.66,
          "en": "to check if isAuthenticating is true,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 202.66,
          "end": 206.23,
          "en": "and if it is, we don't wanna return this authContent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 206.23,
          "end": 207.75,
          "en": "but, instead, I will return",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 207.75,
          "end": 211.43,
          "en": "my LoadingOverlay component here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 211.43,
          "end": 215.45,
          "en": "which is defined in the LoadingOverlay file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 215.45,
          "end": 218.18,
          "en": "and we need to import this component for that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 218.18,
          "end": 221.63,
          "en": "So, import LoadingOverlay from the components folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 221.63,
          "end": 226.27,
          "en": "from the UI folder, and then the LoadingOverlay file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 226.27,
          "end": 229.54,
          "en": "And this LoadingOverlay component wants a message prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 229.54,
          "end": 231.18,
          "en": "which is shown on the screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 231.18,
          "end": 235.54,
          "en": "therefore, actually here, we wanna set this message prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 235.54,
          "end": 237.76,
          "en": "and set it to any message of your choice,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 237.76,
          "end": 241.097,
          "en": "like, for example, \"Creating user dot, dot, dot\".",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 243.04,
          "end": 245.47,
          "en": "Now with that, we should have the basics we need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 245.47,
          "end": 249.99,
          "en": "for sending a request to this, Create A User end point,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 249.99,
          "end": 251.83,
          "en": "and for showing a loading spinner",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 251.83,
          "end": 254.263,
          "en": "whilst the request is on its way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 255.19,
          "end": 259.06,
          "en": "If I now save everything, I get an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 259.06,
          "end": 262.71,
          "en": "Yeah, because \"UI\" should actually be lower case here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 262.71,
          "end": 266.037,
          "en": "Alternatively, you rename this to an upper case folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 266.037,
          "end": 270.3,
          "en": "but with that, if I now save this and I force a reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 270.3,
          "end": 272.57,
          "en": "this reloads successfully.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 272.57,
          "end": 274.1,
          "en": "And now, if we create a user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 274.1,
          "end": 276.85,
          "en": "we wanna enter a valid email address here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 276.85,
          "end": 280.04,
          "en": "You can, of course also test if invalid data is caught,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 280.04,
          "end": 281.87,
          "en": "but it should be.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 281.87,
          "end": 284.24,
          "en": "And enter a valid password that is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 284.24,
          "end": 285.71,
          "en": "at least seven characters long,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 285.71,
          "end": 287.83,
          "en": "so more than six characters,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 287.83,
          "end": 290.65,
          "en": "and if you then click \"Signup\", you see this loading spinner",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 290.65,
          "end": 292.57,
          "en": "and then we go back to this screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 292.57,
          "end": 294.793,
          "en": "That is the behavior we have at the moment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 296.09000000000003,
          "end": 297.78,
          "en": "But now let's check our backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 297.78,
          "end": 300.9,
          "en": "and see if a user was created.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 300.9,
          "end": 305.02,
          "en": "For this here, we can go back to the Authentication area",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 305.02,
          "end": 307.4,
          "en": "in Firebase, and you should now see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 307.4,
          "end": 310.22,
          "en": "a new user entry here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 310.22,
          "end": 312.313,
          "en": "with the email address you chose.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 314.11,
          "end": 317.18,
          "en": "It also has an ID which was automatically generated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 317.18,
          "end": 318.92,
          "en": "and assigned by Firebase,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 318.92,
          "end": 322.17,
          "en": "and the existence of this user now proves",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 322.17,
          "end": 325.39,
          "en": "that our general authentication flow",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 325.39,
          "end": 329.85,
          "en": "or the user creation flow, to be precise, works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 329.85,
          "end": 333.7,
          "en": "Therefore, as a next step, we can work on logging users in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 333.7,
          "end": 337.103,
          "en": "and sending a request to that API endpoint.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
